## Codebase Patterns

- `tsconfig.json` maps the bare specifier `fflate` to `./src/index.ts`, so
  node tests can `import { x } from 'fflate'` and get the SOURCE, no build
  needed. `test/3-node-min.ts` is the exception: it deliberately imports
  `../dist/node/index{,.min}.js` to cover the shipped bundles.
- The node suite is a set of numerically-prefixed files that `test/index.ts`
  imports in order. Adding a new file means adding its import there too --
  tapzero has no CLI runner, so an unimported file simply never runs.
- Run one file at a time with `npx tsx test/<file>.ts`. Files that only
  export a suite function (everything under `test/browser/`) cannot be run
  this way; see the temporary-entry recipe in the mission prompt.
- To sanity-check something against a built bundle, write a real `.mjs`
  file at the repo root and run `node ./tmp-x.mjs`. Never
  `node --input-type=module -e` -- it poisons worker `execArgv` (CLAUDE.md).
- `npm run lint` prints a `@stylistic` deprecation warning about
  `type-annotation-spacing` on every run. It is pre-existing noise, not a
  failure; exit code 0 is the signal.
- `tsc --noEmit` has `listFiles: true`, so a passing run still prints
  hundreds of paths. Grep for `error TS` rather than reading the tail.
- Worker payloads: `bInflt`/`bDflt` (`src/index.ts`) list the values shipped
  into a worker. `wcln` parses the TEXT of those array literals for the
  identifier names, stringifies anything callable, and posts everything
  else as data. Any value a stringified function references at runtime must
  appear in the array by name, or the worker gets a ReferenceError. Note
  that `bDflt` does NOT contain `err`, and does not need to -- the deflate
  worker path never throws a FlateError.

