## 2026-08-08 - US-003 Expose external file attributes and isDirectory

- `zh` (src/index.ts) now also returns the external file attributes dword
  at central-directory offset `b + 38`. Added a module-level `isdir(at, fn)`
  helper and two new `UnzipFileInfo` members, `attrs:number` and
  `isDirectory:boolean`, wired into the filter object literals in BOTH
  `unzip` and `unzipSync` in the same change.
- Added `test/6-unzip-attrs.ts` (24 assertions) and imported it from
  `test/index.ts`. Documented the new fields in the README filter example.
- Files changed: `src/index.ts`, `test/index.ts`, `test/6-unzip-attrs.ts`,
  `README.md`, `specs/prd.json`, `progress.log`.

- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - The central directory record layout, from the record start: sig 0,
    version made by 4, version needed 6, flags 8, method 10, dostime 12,
    crc 16, csize 20, usize 24, fnlen 28, extralen 30, commentlen 32,
    disk 34, internal attrs 36, EXTERNAL ATTRS 38, local header offset 42,
    filename 46. `zh` already read most of these; only 38 was unused.
  - `b4` is UNSIGNED, so any unix `st_mode` in the high half comes back
    above 2^31. `attrs` is deliberately left unsigned to match. A test that
    computes its expectation as `0o100644 << 16` gets a NEGATIVE number and
    fails -- use `(m << 16) >>> 0`. Same trap applies to `isdir`, which
    uses `at >>> 16` for that reason.
  - `zh` returns an `as const` tuple destructured at exactly two call sites
    (`unzip`, `unzipSync`). Appending to the tuple is safe; both sites must
    still be edited together because of the declaration-emit invariant in
    CLAUDE.md. Confirmed: `tsc --emitDeclarationOnly` is what catches a
    missed one, not the runtime tests.
  - `zipSync` writes 0 into external file attributes for every entry, so it
    cannot produce a fixture that exercises the DOS or unix bits. The test
    builds an archive with `zipSync(..., {level:0})` and then patches
    `o + 38` in each central-directory record via a `DataView`, walking
    from the EOCD. That keeps the fixture a real, tool-readable ZIP with no
    binary blob checked in.
  - The streaming `Unzip`/`UnzipFile` path does NOT go through `zh` -- it
    reads LOCAL file headers, which have no external attributes field at
    all. US-004 will need a different source for `isDirectory` there.
  - Verified: `npx tsx test/6-unzip-attrs.ts` (24/24), full `npm test`
    (node 92/92, browser 322/322), `npm run lint`, `tsc --noEmit` against
    both `tsconfig.json` and `tsconfig.build.json`. Also confirmed the new
    test fails 21/24 with `src/index.ts` stashed.

