- Expanded the doc comments on `FlateStreamHandler` and
  `AsyncFlateStreamHandler` (`src/index.ts`) with the emission contract:
  the handler may be called any number of times including zero, a small
  input is not guaranteed to produce exactly one call, consumers must
  CONCATENATE chunks rather than capture one, and exactly one call has
  `final: true` and it is always the last.
- Added a hand-maintained `## Unreleased` section to `CHANGELOG.md`
  recording the 0.8.3 emission change and the US-008 fix, plus a comment
  warning that `auto-changelog` regenerates from the first release
  heading down, so hand-written notes must stay above it.
- Files changed: `src/index.ts`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `specs/prd.json`,
  `progress.log`.
- No test was written. This story is documentation only: it adds no
  runtime behavior, and the behavior it describes is already covered by
  `test/8-stream-chunks.ts` from US-008. Per execution rule 3, skipping
  test-first here and saying so.

- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - `CHANGELOG.md` is GENERATED by `auto-changelog` from git history --
    the header says so. It rebuilds every `## [vX.Y.Z]` section from the
    first release heading downward. Hand-written content survives only
    ABOVE that first heading, which is where the `Unreleased` section
    now lives. Do not put hand notes between release sections.
  - Verified the claim before writing it rather than assuming the US-008
    fix generalised. `Inflate.c`'s guard covers DECOMPRESSION only;
    `Deflate.p` calls `ondata` unconditionally. Measured the compressors
    with a scratch `tmp-chk.ts`: `Deflate`/`Gzip`/`Zlib` each emitted
    exactly `[[n, true]]` for `push(data)`, `push(empty)`,
    `push(empty, true)` -- i.e. the two intermediate pushes emitted ZERO
    callbacks. That is the concrete evidence for "may be called zero
    times", and it is why the empty-chunk sentence is scoped to
    "a streaming decompressor" rather than claimed for all streams.
  - Typedoc `{@link X}` works in these comments; the async handler's doc
    links back to `FlateStreamHandler` instead of duplicating the prose.
    Do NOT run `npm run build-docs` to check it (CLAUDE.md forbids it --
    it writes over `docs/`, which also holds implementation plans).
  - Verified: `npm run lint` (exit 0), `tsc --noEmit` against both
    `tsconfig.json` and `tsconfig.build.json` (no `error TS`), `npm test`
    full suite (346/346, plain and minified), and a grep for em dashes
